          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On November 28, 1991, around 10:30 PM, at least 25 witnesses across the Atlantic coast and southwest France observed a very bright, green ball traveling at high speed without sound for approximately ten seconds. According to some accounts, the ball disintegrated into a spray of sparks. The general direction inferred from the testimonies appears to be southeast to northwest. It is highly likely that this was the atmospheric reentry of a space debris fragment.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "8e8a9fcd7147b1251464ac65cf4e402e054b8ad7c30ad58ddc0edae203d9e753"
        }
